# The required-arm pin (MAJOR5, #311; review-0.9-m0-s19). tests/run.mjs
# discovers arms by walking the directory - that is deliberate (see its
# own header, "DERIVE, DO NOT PIN") and stays true for the SET of arms
# that exist. What discovery cannot see is a whole arm SUBTRACTED:
# `git rm tests/claim-vs-diff.test.mjs` shrinks the walk by one file and
# the runner simply runs one fewer program, silently green, exit 0 -
# the fewer-checks-and-nobody-noticed failure #204 already found once
# from the other side (a renamed extension leaving arms uncounted).
#
# This file is the independent fact: every path listed below MUST be
# present among what discovery finds, or the gate is red and names
# which one is missing. It is committed and walked on its own, never
# generated from the same directory sweep it is checked against - a
# roster derived from tests/ at read time would shrink with tests/ and
# prove nothing a deletion could not evade.
#
# Adding an arm: `git add` under tests/ already registers it with the
# runner (that half needs no edit here). Add its path below in the same
# commit, so the roster and the arm land together and neither can be
# forgotten - tests/ci-wiring.test.mjs checks CI wiring the same
# both-halves way. Retiring an arm with its surface (the M2/M3/M4
# pattern tests/run.mjs's own header describes) removes its line here
# in the same commit that deletes the file.
#
# THE OTHER DIRECTION (0.9-M3-S1, #381; tests/roster-two-way.test.mjs
# proves it by mutation). The paragraph above is direction A: a row
# naming a file that is gone. Direction B is the one that went
# unchecked until this ticket - a file discovery finds with no row at
# all, whether because a row was deleted (0.9-M2-S14's own review did
# exactly that to prove the gap) or because the file arrived and nobody
# added one. tests/run.mjs now reds on that too, for every
# tests/*.test.mjs it finds that is neither required below nor
# explicitly excluded.
#
# A suite that is deliberately non-gating is written down, not just
# left off: add a line reading
#     EXCLUDE <path> :: <reason>
# A path with no "::" after it, or an empty reason, is its own red
# (MALFORMED EXCLUSION) rather than a silent no-op - and it does not
# excuse the suite it names. An exclusion for a file discovery cannot
# find is its own red too (STALE EXCLUSION) - delete the line with the
# file. A path both required and excluded is a contradiction
# (REQUIRED AND EXCLUDED) - pick one.
#
# A roster with zero required rows is empty and reds (ROSTER (empty)),
# NO MATTER HOW MANY EXCLUDE LINES it carries (0.9-M3-S7, #410) - an
# exclusion count never substitutes for a requirement. And a line
# repeated - the same required path twice, or the same path EXCLUDEd
# twice, even with two different reasons - is its own red too
# (DUPLICATE REQUIRED ROW, DUPLICATE EXCLUSION): a second EXCLUDE line
# would otherwise silently overwrite the first's reason, which is the
# same silent state this whole file exists to refuse.
#
# One required path per line, repo-relative, forward-slashed, plus the
# EXCLUDE lines above - each path named at most once, either way.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

